//fldigi macro definition file extended
// =============================================================================
// Description: Contest macros for DARC Worked All Europe DX Contest (WAEDC), RTTY
// WAEDC Rules: https://www.darc.de/der-club/referate/conteste/wae-dx-contest/en/wae-rules/
//
// EXCHANGE = RST SERIAL (001, 002, ...)
//
// BEFORE THE CONTEST (lessons from 2026):
// - fldigi: Contest = Generic contest, serial numbers on (start 1, 3 digits,
//   leading zeros). TAB OUT of Start, then press Reset (#Out must show 001).
//   RST always 599. Tick Band in the dupe check (each station once per band).
// - Disconnect the N3FJP link: while connected, #Out shows N3FJP's number,
//   which can differ from what <CNTR> sends.
// - Logbook > QTC Manager > Reset QTCs after any testing.
// - New logbook for the contest.
//
// DURING THE CONTEST:
// - Log ONLY with macro 6. Any other way skips <INCR> and repeats a serial.
// - Check Serial # In before logging (2026: one QSO logged with my own serial).
// - Tags after </EXEC> are not run, so <EXEC> is always last in a macro.
// - QTCs go between different continents only: anyone outside North America
//   (Caribbean, Central America and Greenland are North America).
// - Up to 10 QTCs per station pair, sent plus received. Check View QTCs.
// - Send QTCs ONLY with QTC Manager TX > Send all QTC (it sends the header).
//   Per-row TX QTC is for repeats only, and wait for each to finish.
// - Receive: type each dashed line (0745-JG8JBX-28) into QTC Manager RX, Save.
// - Calling: after 3-4 unanswered calls, move on and come back later.
//
// WHAT THE OTHER STATIONS SAID (2026):
// - "DO YOU WANT QTC?" / "QTC?"  = they offer to send       -> macro 18
// - "SEND ME QTC" / "QTC FOR ME?" = they want mine          -> macro 16
// - "QTC RX/TX?" / "WANT/HAVE QTC?" = which way?            -> 16 or 18
// - Sender: "QTC 37/10 R U QRV? BK"; receiver: "QRV PSE GO" / "I AM QRV BK"
// - Receiver: "R R R ALL OK BK" or "AGN QTC 7 7 7" or "AGN HEADER"
//
// AFTER THE CONTEST:
// - Fix the frequency (band you sent on) and mode (RY) of sent QTC lines in
//   qtc-log.tsv or the Cabrillo file; delete any series never confirmed.
// - Fill in the Cabrillo header; fldigi leaves the categories blank.
// - Upload: dxhf2.darc.de/~waerttylog/upload.cgi (deadline one week later).
//
// Brian McLaughlin (N3BMC) <n3bmc@arrl.net>
//
// History:
// Date       Initials Notes
// ---------- -------- ---------------------------------------------------------
// 2026-11-13 BMC      Created from the JARL WW RTTY macros written for 2026
// 2026-11-15 BMC      2027 starter: lessons from WAE RTTY 2026, QTC phrasing,
//                     <EXEC> moved last in Log, file-based QTC fallback removed
//
// =============================================================================

// Row 1 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Macro # 1
/$ 0 CQ @#+
<TX>\n
CQ CQ WAE <MYCALL> <MYCALL> CQ\n
<RX><AFTER:10>

//
// Macro # 2
/$ 1 Resp @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> 599 <CNTR> <CNTR> <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 3
/$ 2 Run @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU GL <MYCALL> CQ\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 4
/$ 3 Stop @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 5
/$ 4 QRT @>|
<TX>\n
DE <MYCALL> QRT QRT DE <MYCALL> SK\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 6
// Log, advance the serial, then upload. <EXEC> must stay last.
/$ 5  Log
<LOG><INCR><EXEC>fltools clublog</EXEC>

//
// Macro # 7
// Run: close the QSO and ask which way QTCs go (non-NA stations only)
/$ 6 TU QTC? @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU WANT/HAVE QTC? <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 8
/$ 7 

//
// Macro # 9
/$ 8 

//
// Macro # 10
/$ 9 

//
// Macro # 11
/$ 10 Tx @>>
<TX>\n

//
// Macro # 12
/$ 11 Rx @||
\n
<RX>

// Row 2 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Macro # 13
/$ 12 SP Hunt @>|
<TX>\n
<MYCALL> <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 14
/$ 13 SP Ans @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU 599 <CNTR> <CNTR> <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 15
// S&P: answer and ask which way QTCs go (non-NA stations only)
/$ 14 SP Ans QTC? @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU 599 <CNTR> <CNTR> WANT/HAVE QTC? <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 16
// QTC sending: they want mine. Ask if ready, then QTC Manager TX > Send all QTC.
/$ 15 Have QTC @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> I HAVE QTC FOR YOU R U QRV? BK\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 17
// QTC sending: other station confirmed (R R R ALL OK / QSL ALL)
/$ 16 QTC TU @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> TU QSL QTC GL <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 18
// QTC receiving: they offered QTCs. Then open QTC Manager RX.
/$ 17 QTC QRV @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> I AM QRV PSE GO BK\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 19
// QTC receiving: all lines copied. Then Save in QTC Manager RX.
/$ 18 QSL ALL @>|
<TX>\n
R R R ALL OK QSL ALL TU <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 20
// QTC receiving: starts TX; type the line number three times and BK
// (for example "7 7 7 BK"), then press Rx
/$ 19 QTC AGN @>>
<TX>\n
AGN QTC 

//
// Macro # 21
// QTC receiving: header not copied
/$ 20 AGN HDR @>|
<TX>\n
AGN HEADER AGN HEADER BK\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 22
// Decline QTCs: both stations in North America, or 10 already exchanged
/$ 21 No QTC @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> SRI NO QTC TU <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 23
/$ 22 

//
// Macro # 24
/$ 23 

// Row 3 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Macro # 25
/$ 24 Full Repeat @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> 599 <CNTR> <CNTR> <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 26
/$ 25 RST Repeat @>|
<TX>\n
599 599\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 27
/$ 26 NR Repeat @>|
<TX>\n
<CNTR> <CNTR>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 28
/$ 27 

//
// Macro # 29
/$ 28 

//
// Macro # 30
/$ 29 

//
// Macro # 31
/$ 30 

//
// Macro # 32
/$ 31 

//
// Macro # 33
/$ 32 Feld Hell
<MODEM:FELDHELL>
<RIGMODE:USB-D>
<RXRSID:off>
<TXRSID:off>
<MACROS:/Users/brian/.fldigi/macros/hell_macros.mdf>

//
// Macro # 34
/$ 33 Olivia 8-250
<MODEM:OLIVIA:250:8>
<RIGMODE:USB-D>
<RXRSID:on>
<TXRSID:on>
<MACROS:/Users/brian/.fldigi/macros/olivia_macros.mdf>

//
// Macro # 35
/$ 34 PSK
<MODEM:BPSK31>
<RIGMODE:USB-D>
<RXRSID:on>
<TXRSID:on>
<MACROS:/Users/brian/.fldigi/macros/psk_macros.mdf>

//
// Macro # 36
/$ 35 RTTY
<MODEM:RTTY:170:45.45:5>
<RIGMODE:RTTY>
<RXRSID:off>
<TXRSID:off>
<MACROS:/Users/brian/.fldigi/macros/rtty_macros.mdf>

// Row 4 -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Macro # 37
/$ 36 AGN? @>|
<TX>\n
AGN AGN?\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 38
/$ 37 RST? @>|
<TX>\n
RST RST?\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 39
/$ 38 NR? @>|
<TX>\n
NR NR?\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 40
/$ 39 CALL? @>|
<TX>\n
CALL CALL?\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 41
/$ 40 QTC? @>|
<TX>\n
<CALL> WANT/HAVE QTC? <MYCALL>\n
<RX>

//
// Macro # 42
/$ 41 

//
// Macro # 43
// Open the fltools log in Console, which follows new lines as they are written
/$ 42 fltools Log
<EXEC>open -a Console "$HOME/Library/Logs/fltools/fltools.log" >/dev/null 2>&1 &</EXEC>

//
// Macro # 44
/$ 43 Entry to ClubLog
<EXEC>fltools clublog</EXEC>

//
// Macro # 45
/$ 44 Entry to QRZ
<EXEC>fltools qrz</EXEC>

//
// Macro # 46
/$ 45 CLR Tx
<CLRTX>

//
// Macro # 47
/$ 46 CLR Rx
<CLRRX>

//
// Macro # 48
/$ 47 CLRALL
<CLRRX><CLRTX>
